obo:FLOPO_0980586 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete obsolete cream sensu RHS Colour Chart fifth edition"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "OBSOLETE. A colour quality for which RHS Colour Chart fifth-edition chip 158A or 158B is the specimen's closest visual match against a white background under artificial daylight conforming to CIE D6500."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Obsoleted by the ISCC-NBS colour backbone (curator decision 2026-09-18): FLOPO keeps only ISCC-NBS level-1 to level-3 colour classes, and colour words become botanical_colour_name synonyms. Consider 'yellow (ISCC-NBS level 2)' (FLOPO:0988019); the former label is now a synonym of that class."@en,
        "Use only when the observation or protocol names RHS fifth-edition chip 158A or 158B. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104031 (cream). Move this source-specific referent to a new FLOPO class; PATO:0104031 remains the generic cream parent."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf> ;
    oboInOwl:consider obo:FLOPO_0988019 ;
    owl:deprecated true .

obo:FLOPO_0980587 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete obsolete cream sensu Saccardo (1891)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "OBSOLETE. A colour quality recognized according to Saccardo's Chromotaxia as category 27, represented by cow-milk cream and described as white tinged faintly with yellow."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Obsoleted by the ISCC-NBS colour backbone (curator decision 2026-09-18): FLOPO keeps only ISCC-NBS level-1 to level-3 colour classes, and colour words become botanical_colour_name synonyms. Consider 'yellow (ISCC-NBS level 2)' (FLOPO:0988019); the former label is now a synonym of that class."@en,
        "Use only when Saccardo's nomenclature or category 27 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104031 (cream). The natural exemplar varies; the historical plate/category is the source-specific reference."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/chromotaxiaseuno00sacc> ;
    oboInOwl:consider obo:FLOPO_0988019 ;
    owl:deprecated true .

obo:FLOPO_0980588 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete obsolete crimson sensu Wilson Horticultural Colour Chart (1938/1940)"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "OBSOLETE. A colour quality recognized according to the Wilson Horticultural Colour Chart by closest match to chip H22, which the NIST source concordance places in ISCC-NBS block 11 vivid red."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Obsoleted by the ISCC-NBS colour backbone (curator decision 2026-09-18): FLOPO keeps only ISCC-NBS level-1 to level-3 colour classes, and colour words become botanical_colour_name synonyms. Consider 'vivid red' (FLOPO:0988038); the former label is now a synonym of that class."@en,
        "Use only when the Wilson chart or H22 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104314 (crimson). ISCC-NBS block 11 is a concordance classification, not a replacement for the physical H22 prototype."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.6028/NBS.SP.440>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.061.035> ;
    oboInOwl:consider obo:FLOPO_0988038 ;
    owl:deprecated true .

obo:FLOPO_0980589 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obsolete obsolete crimson sensu Textile Color Card Association of the USA"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "OBSOLETE. A colour quality recognized according to the Textile Color Card Association of the USA by closest match to card 65013, which the NIST source concordance places in ISCC-NBS block 256 deep purplish red."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Obsoleted by the ISCC-NBS colour backbone (curator decision 2026-09-18): FLOPO keeps only ISCC-NBS level-1 to level-3 colour classes, and colour words become botanical_colour_name synonyms. Consider 'deep purplish red' (PATO:0104087); the former label is now a synonym of that class."@en,
        "Use only when TCCA card 65013 is specified. FLOPO-local source-qualified colour quality; its generic colour is PATO:0104314 (crimson). This sense demonstrates why crimson cannot be assigned one unrestricted red prototype."@en ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-07-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-09-18"^^xsd:date ;
